{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-categorical-fourier-brings-dft","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:categorical-fourier-brings-dft","kind":"remark","title":"Abelian instance: the Bring's-surface DFT and Briggs--Klein smoothness","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-fourier","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-briggs-klein-chart","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-lagrange-resolvents","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-brings-smoothness"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-fourier","tags":["fourier","dft","bring-surface","briggs-klein","lagrange-resolvent"],"text":"categorical-fourier-brings-dft.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:categorical-fourier-brings-dft\"></a><p>When <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G = C_5</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>, the transform degenerates to the classical discrete Fourier transform on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}/5</code>. Fourier decomposition separates spectral components, rendering collision invisible and securing the smoothness of the Briggs--Klein chart on Bring's surface.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-brings-dft.md","heading":"Remark","number":"4.21.14","page":"b/rem-categorical-fourier-brings-dft","qa":{"counts":{"pass":57,"fail":0,"warn":2,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":1}}}
